{
 "version": 1,
 "description": "Everyday phrasings of an errand request, as people type them, and what the parser must make of each. `expect` lists the errand categories that must be found (order free); an open need counts by its category hint. `reject` means the text is not an errand and must not become one. `walking` / `preferred_brand` check that a preference stayed a preference. `set` is `tuned` for the phrasings the parser was fixed against and `held_out` for ones written afterwards and never tuned for; the held-out rate is the honest one. Scored by tools/evaluate_phrasings.py against the built catalog. Optional checks: `exact_brand` / `excluded_brand` (a negated brand must be excluded, never asked for), `optional` (the categories that must be optional), `modifier` (e.g. takeaway), `arrival_time` (HH:MM, Singapore), `max_detour` / `detour_hard`, `not_understood` (terms that must be reported back rather than dropped) and `spelling` (a fuzzy match must be reported as a correction).",
